WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.910
Hey guys, Pete here. This will be my
better Call Saul season 5 episode 10

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.110
recap and review. I've got to mention
that this will be spoilery contains

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.150
spoilers for everything that's happened
in better Call Saul through season 5 and

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.890
also cover events through the entire run
of Breaking Bad. if you're not caught up

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:24.539
then this is your chance to turn away.
The season 5 finale was titled "Something

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:28.650
Unforgivable" and it brought what was
arguably the best season of Better Call

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.329
Saul to a close. In doing that it felt
more like a setup for the ending rather

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:37.739
than an end. And in this case it worked
well, but I wouldn't say it was

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:42.660
satisfying. Then again I'm not sure it
would have felt satisfying if any of the

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.789
major characters whose endings we don't
know came to an end either. Overall I

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:51.180
didn't want it to end but it did. I want
answers,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.070
but as Mike would say I'm asking for
information I can't have. I like where we

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.600
are, but I don't like the uncertainty of
not knowing when we'll actually get to

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.000
see the final season. What I do know is
Kim and Jimmy have switched places from

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.470
where we left them at the end of season
4. In that closing scene Kim was surprised

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:15.119
to learn that Jimmy had fooled everyone
including her with his passionate speech

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:19.530
about the law and his brother in his
reinstatement hearing. We watch him walk

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.030
down the hall emboldened by all the
recent events. Stopping to turn with a

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.710
smile to say, "it's all good man." As he
goes we see this shot of Kim as the

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.119
camera pulls away where she's looking
lost and alone. To make it worse Jimmy

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:37.320
seems to be clueless about how his
future wife feels in that moment. In the

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.790
season 5 finale the tables are turned.
Jimmy is still recovering from the

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.810
shootout in the desert and the opening
of the episode he finally comes clean

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.310
about what actually happened. the
couple decide to head to a fancy hotel

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:55.470
to distance themselves from the scene of
Lalo's unexpected drop in. Jimmy feels

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.939
relieved after Mike tells him that Lalo
will be killed, but he's far from

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:03.899
emboldened this time around. when she
comes up with the plan to destroy

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:09.569
Howard's career so that they can force
Sandpiper to settle, it's Kim who seems

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:13.530
to be clueless about where her
partners head is at. the shows co-creator

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.989
Peter Gould who directed and co-wrote
this episode with Ariel Levine really

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:23.310
leaned into this connection between
these two scenes. when Jimmy was walking

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.660
away he turned and pointed in Kim's
direction with two fingers. when Kim

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.530
walks away she turns and makes a finger
gun gesture shooting in Jimmy's

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.849
direction. this time we watched the
camera pull away from Jimmy and he's the

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:40.230
one who looks lost and alone as he sits
on the bed trying to wrap his head

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:45.150
around what he just heard. the turnaround
is surprising, but not completely out of

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:50.010
the blue. what I really loved about the
way it played out inside the episode was

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:53.940
watching the progression. when they first
came to the hotel we could tell that

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.840
they were dealing with what happened in
different ways. Kim was up early in the

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.370
morning ready to hit the courthouse.
Jimmy tries to stop her from going and

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:06.120
we get the sense that he just wants to
hide. we can look at their screen time

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:11.280
together and apart as an examination of
how each of them reacts to this

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.250
traumatic experience that they just went
through together.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.359
Kim loads up on cases at the public
defender's office before she runs into

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:22.470
Howard. Jimmy goes looking for Mike to
get answers about how worried they

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.549
should be. I think the most telling
moment for Kim is her laughing in

00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:31.079
Howard's face after she learns about the
bowling balls and prostitutes, it all

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:35.190
sounds like small potatoes to a person
who just talked her way out of a

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:40.350
showdown with a cartel boss. for Jimmy
it's when we see his anger drop as he

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:45.660
says, "if anything happens to her," to Mike.
to be fair Jimmy probably should be in a

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.950
worse spot considering his experience in
the desert, but by the time they come

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:55.250
back together at the hotel we understand
that their heads are in different places.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.329
Slippin' Jimmy can't help himself when
talk turns to a scam though. things start

00:04:00.329 --> 00:04:04.799
out innocently enough with Kim joking
about shaving Howard's head and of

00:04:04.799 --> 00:04:08.880
course Jimmy knows a much better way to
go about it. we see the progression kick

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.829
in from there. things snowball and as the
tables turn to Jimmy trying to put on

00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:18.690
the brakes it all feels inevitable. even
though she's telling herself she's doing

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:24.120
it for the right reasons, and the cost is
only a career setback for one lawyer, we

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.810
know that
final price will probably be well beyond

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:32.550
whatever worst case scenario she might
be thinking. we are in the Breaking Bad

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.199
universe after all, and that's a place
where choices come with consequences.

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:41.639
even in my initial reaction of having
just watched the episode there are so

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:46.710
many different possibilities flying
around in my mind. questions like, "did Kim

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:51.900
just break bad?" "was this always about Kim
Breaking Bad?" "is there something in Kim's

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.800
history that we don't know about where
she's already done this sort of thing?"

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.479
where does that leave Jimmy? will he feel
responsible? will he try to protect her?

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:05.580
will a feeling of responsibility cause
him to intervene and try to derail their

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:11.280
plans in a way to protect her? it opens a
lot of doors without really negating the

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.180
ideas we've already had about where
things are heading. I'll come back to

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.650
that at the end because we still have
the whole cartel story to talk about.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:23.400
we learned that after leaving the
apartment Lalo and Nacho did go straight

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.600
to the border and watch them arrive at
Lalo's compound. he's welcomed by his

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.380
staff and I instantly feared for all of
their lives.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.460
going into this episode I had a hard
time imagining any of the major

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:40.110
characters dying, but when the camera
lingered on his cook outside of Lalo's

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:44.370
home it just felt like she was a goner.
that worked well to set up the ending

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.690
and the trip to Don Eladio's with
Nacho being able to impress him really

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:53.400
had me thinking Lalo might die.
the trip to Don Eladio's really

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.870
scratched the Breaking Bad references
itch. this time around we watched Lalo

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.370
score some points for the Salamanca
family over Gus who came up a little bit

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:05.820
short.
Lalo gifts Eladio a Magnum PI style

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.919
Ferrari with a big box of cash in the
"frunk". Nacho is able to win him over in

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:15.900
their conversation which is capped off
with a "salud". this of course is the title

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:20.669
of the Breaking Bad episode where Gus
finally gets his revenge against Eladio

00:06:20.669 --> 00:06:25.560
and the other cartel bosses. back at
Lalo's compound we see Gus's

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:30.449
assassination plot play out.
Nacho got a call instructing him to open

00:06:30.449 --> 00:06:34.710
the back gate. when he goes to do that
Lalo is sitting by the fire drinking a

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.409
beer.
Nacho has to think

00:06:36.409 --> 00:06:41.479
fast and makes things work by causing a
diversion with a frying pan of oil on

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:46.099
the stove when he goes inside to get
more to drink. Lalo has to do some fast

00:06:46.099 --> 00:06:49.999
thinking of his own when the assassins
show up outside the kitchen. with the

00:06:49.999 --> 00:06:53.839
help of a human shield he makes his way
to his tunnel that he has in his

00:06:53.839 --> 00:06:58.429
bathroom. my favorite part of this was
him stopping just as he was about to

00:06:58.429 --> 00:07:03.469
close it. we see that he comes up with
this plan to come back in that moment. he

00:07:03.469 --> 00:07:07.369
knows that they'll try to follow him and
uses this to his advantage when he

00:07:07.369 --> 00:07:11.479
sneaks back into the house.
Nacho is able to get away but he ends up

00:07:11.479 --> 00:07:16.219
by himself since all the assassins are
taken out. in a great shot Lalo pulls

00:07:16.219 --> 00:07:21.050
the mask off the guy he burned with the
oil and tells him to call his bosses to

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:25.429
tell them that the job is done. he looks
over and sees the decanter that Nacho

00:07:25.429 --> 00:07:29.689
had brought out before he gets up. then
he sees the dead body of his favorite

00:07:29.689 --> 00:07:34.339
cook as he's walking away. as he goes it
looks like the rage is building up

00:07:34.339 --> 00:07:40.159
inside him as the episode and the season
come to a close. and that's where we

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:44.929
leave things. besides that last sequence
it was a mostly subdued episode in

00:07:44.929 --> 00:07:49.339
comparison to the wild ride that
episodes six through nine were, but it's

00:07:49.339 --> 00:07:54.110
not like things slowed down. let's look
at where all the characters are. Gus, and

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:59.300
by extension Mike, will surely be in a
tough spot after this. Lalo will know it

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:04.099
was Gus that sent these guys and he's
just won favor with Don Eladio. Gus's

00:08:04.099 --> 00:08:08.479
best option will be to try to pin it on
Nacho, but he may run into some

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:12.709
resistance from Mike. for Nacho himself
he's gonna have to figure out a way to

00:08:12.709 --> 00:08:17.569
stay alive after fleeing the compound in
the short term he may be able to get

00:08:17.569 --> 00:08:22.669
away perhaps the assassins left a driver
or at least their vehicles behind but

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:27.649
what options does he have after that as
for Lalo beyond the people inside his

00:08:27.649 --> 00:08:32.599
house he didn't lose much his biggest
problem is that Gus is in the US and

00:08:32.599 --> 00:08:36.680
he's wanted there for murder and jumping
bail he'll have to figure out how to

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:41.269
deal with Nacho but his position isn't
weakened that much on the other side of

00:08:41.269 --> 00:08:45.829
things Kim appears to be set on going
after Howard she's convinced herself

00:08:45.829 --> 00:08:48.490
that the good she can do with the money
is worth

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:52.480
whatever harm they have to hand out in
the process of getting it Howard looks

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:56.380
poised to play a much bigger role next
season and I'm not sure he's ready for

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:01.240
the fight that he's in for Jimmy and Kim
are a pretty formidable duo when they

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.810
start working together
when Jimmy mentioned the episode title

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.589
and saying that it would take something
unforgivable to get them to turn on

00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:13.209
Howard he quickly followed that up by
saying he doesn't deserve that which is

00:09:13.209 --> 00:09:17.950
true Howard has his problems he's not
the greatest human being but it's coming

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.610
to Kim wasn't as much about him as she
made it out to be

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:26.080
Howard's concern that Jimmy needs help
is actually true Howard thinks he needs

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.890
help and he actually does need help
and Howard delivered one of the best

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:35.080
lines of the episode when he said, "you
know who really knew Jimmy? Chuck" and for

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.580
my money it's not just because this is a
great way to shut down the conversation

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.810
but because it highlights Kim's
inability to see the situation

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:48.130
objectively Kim got duped by Jimmy in
that Mesa Verde meeting and she decided

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:52.810
to solve the problem by getting married
everything we've seen her do since then

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.640
has been to prove to herself that this
was the right decision in their private

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:02.260
life she only has the choice of doubling
down or walking away and to this point

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:07.270
we've seen no hints at her leaving I
don't want to sound sour on Kim I loved

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.470
the character of Kim and the betrayal by
Rhea Seehorn. Rhea Seehorn needs to win

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.680
an Emmy this year as far as I'm
concerned I'm not saying that she

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.160
doesn't care for Jimmy or that they
shouldn't have gotten together really

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:22.329
I'm just saying that her decision to be
all-in with Jimmy coupled with her

00:10:22.329 --> 00:10:26.770
personality and sense of wanting to
solve her problems herself has me

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:31.089
worried I'm not sure if she's emboldened
by getting through the lalo scare if

00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:36.610
she's maybe already been down this road
before or if she's just not able to see

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:40.839
the slippery slope in front of her right
this moment I do know that I've always

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:45.100
been worried about how Jimmy was going
to bring her down and now I'm worried

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:49.660
that she's on the way to doing that
herself we spent all this time wondering

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:54.070
when Jimmy would become the guy we knew
from Breaking Bad and at the end of the

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:58.449
season he looks like he's just along for
the ride at this point that in itself

00:10:58.449 --> 00:11:01.720
may not be satisfying but how we got to
this

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:06.250
they surely has been and the questions
that raises are a lot of fun to think

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:10.540
about it's impossible to say for sure
how things are gonna play out

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:14.620
we got Kim and Lalo both picking up a
head of steam heading towards the finish

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.379
line
Jimmy has his concerns with Kim's plans

00:11:17.379 --> 00:11:22.300
although he'll likely jump in with both
feet once the scam gets going it'll be

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:27.759
interesting to see what Lalo expects him
to do and how much enthusiasm he brings

00:11:27.759 --> 00:11:33.100
along with him we're at the end for now
but it feels more like a pause hopefully

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:37.810
it won't take two years until we get to
find out how it ends but even in the

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:42.519
worst case scenario it'll probably be
worth the wait there were so many great

00:11:42.519 --> 00:11:47.560
small details in this episode I'm just
gonna point out - when she's making the

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.730
sundae at first Jimmy says he wants
everything and then he asks her to take

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:55.870
out the mint chip which it was the same
flavor he had in the ice cream cone when

00:11:55.870 --> 00:12:00.490
Nacho came to pick him up to introduce
him to Lalo for the first time another

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:04.449
one almost feels like a troll from the
writers there's been all this discussion

00:12:04.449 --> 00:12:07.930
about the fact that Jimmy still
terrified of Lalo when we first meet him

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:11.680
in Breaking Bad that's made people think
that he might still be alive later in

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:16.569
the series Gus tells Hector that the
Salamanca name dies with him indicating

00:12:16.569 --> 00:12:21.129
that Lalo is dead at the end of this
episode Lalo made the assassin called

00:12:21.129 --> 00:12:25.779
Gus which at least in the moment would
probably believe him so the water gets

00:12:25.779 --> 00:12:30.009
even muddier because it turns out now
that Gus could actually be wrong

00:12:30.009 --> 00:12:34.120
whenever he thinks he's dead I do think
this was the best season of better call

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:38.379
Saul to date season three had been my
favorite and I think this topped it

00:12:38.379 --> 00:12:42.430
because the two sides of the story
finally came together I loved Chuck as a

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:46.509
character and missed him once he was
gone but I feel like the focus on

00:12:46.509 --> 00:12:50.949
bringing Kim and Lalo front and center
really pays off of course it's all built

00:12:50.949 --> 00:12:55.059
on the character work that they've been
doing in the lead up so on some level it

00:12:55.059 --> 00:12:59.350
just feels like they're getting better
as they go along the writing acting and

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:03.309
filmmaking are all incredibly good at
the moment like I said in my la love

00:13:03.309 --> 00:13:07.870
video I do believe bringing his
character in at the end of season 4

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:13.029
brought life back into the cartel side
of the story and with him bringing Kim

00:13:13.029 --> 00:13:16.889
into that side it
feels like we're approaching an end to

00:13:16.889 --> 00:13:21.479
the series and even though the focus
wasn't on Jimmy at the end it was still

00:13:21.479 --> 00:13:26.129
a great season for the character he got
married he became a friend of the cartel

00:13:26.129 --> 00:13:30.299
and he even drank some of his own pee in
some ways they've only been putting off

00:13:30.299 --> 00:13:34.410
the inevitable with him but I can't
really think of a glaring example of

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:38.429
something that was not essential that
happened this season Bob Odenkirk has

00:13:38.429 --> 00:13:42.569
always been great and I think he's
outdone himself in this season my quick

00:13:42.569 --> 00:13:46.739
take after finishing the episode was
that Jimmy will do something to sabotage

00:13:46.739 --> 00:13:50.939
